# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the key.
#
# `.env` is git-ignored and must never be committed. This file carries names and
# explanations only — never a real value.
#
# Everything except the key is optional. The defaults in
# src/assistant/settings.py are what the published numbers were measured with,
# so overriding one here means the figures in the README no longer describe
# what you are actually running.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required for answering. Retrieval works without it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
#
# `doc-assistant index` and the retrieval half of `doc-assistant eval` run
# without this and cost nothing. Only `ask` and the answering half need it.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — model and cost
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Cost per 1,000 questions at roughly 1,200 input / 200 output tokens:
#   claude-haiku-4-5    $2.20   (default)
#   claude-sonnet-5     $6.60
#   claude-opus-5      $11.00
#
# Haiku is the default because the task is reading four short passages and
# judging whether they answer a question — comprehension rather than reasoning.
# Whether it costs accuracy is a question for `doc-assistant eval`, not for
# intuition.
# ANSWER_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5

# Thinking depth. Leave this unset unless you know why you are setting it.
#
# Not every model accepts it: `effort` is supported on the Opus and Sonnet
# tiers and is REJECTED by Haiku 4.5. Setting it while using the default model
# fails every request with a 400 — a total outage from an optional parameter.
# Only set it alongside an ANSWER_MODEL on a tier that supports it.
# ANSWER_EFFORT=low

# Ceiling on answer length. Enough for a grounded answer with its citations.
# ANSWER_MAX_TOKENS=1024

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — retrieval
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# How many passages are retrieved and put in front of the model.
# RETRIEVAL_TOP_K=4

# Below this similarity, skip the paid call entirely.
#
# This is NOT the refusal mechanism. ADR-0002 measured that no similarity
# threshold separates answerable questions from unanswerable ones: the score
# ranges overlap, so any cutoff either turns away good questions or lets bad
# ones through. Refusal is decided by the model reading the passages.
#
# This exists only to avoid paying for questions with no topical relation at
# all. Keep it well below the lowest observed in-scope score (0.666), or it
# starts rejecting questions the model should have been allowed to read.
# PREFILTER_SCORE=0.45

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — serving a different corpus (per-deployment configuration)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# One image can serve any corpus. These four settings are what turn this from
# "OJ's project" into something deployable for someone else's documents, and
# they are the whole of that difference.

# Where the documents live. Relative to the working directory, or absolute.
# CORPUS_DIR=content

# Refuse to start unless the corpus hashes to this value.
#
# Set it for any deployment whose corpus is authored in another repository and
# copied in. A stale or partially copied corpus is otherwise indistinguishable
# from a correct one until somebody reads an answer carefully — and by then it
# has been answering confidently from the wrong content.
#
# Leave both unset for local work and for a deployment that owns its corpus in
# the same repository: there is nothing to compare against.
# CORPUS_CHECKSUM=

# The same value read from a file, so an exported artifact can carry its own
# digest and a release needs no configuration edit. CORPUS_CHECKSUM wins if both
# are set. Honest limitation: a digest that travels with the corpus it describes
# catches a partial or stale copy, not a substitution of both together.
# CORPUS_CHECKSUM_FILE=

# A file containing this deployment's system prompt — role, tone, scope,
# guardrails, output format, examples. Unset uses the built-in generic
# document-assistant prompt, which is the right default and nobody's assistant.
#
# Per-deployment only. There is no interface for editing it and no request field
# reaches it: a system prompt a caller can influence is not a system prompt.
# SYSTEM_PROMPT_FILE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — restricting who may spend the budget
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Off by default, because the public demo is deliberately open. Turn it on for
# any deployment funded by your own key: without it, anyone who finds the
# hostname can spend that budget, and rate limiting only decides how long they
# need. Callers then present the secret in an `X-Assistant-Secret` header.
#
# Setting REQUIRE_SHARED_SECRET without SHARED_SECRET fails at startup rather
# than serving unauthenticated.
# REQUIRE_SHARED_SECRET=false
# SHARED_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — spend limits
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Paid calls allowed per UTC day. An operational allowance, NOT a monetary
# ceiling: the counter lives in process memory and resets on restart, so under a
# scale-to-zero deployment it resets routinely. Only the provider-side spend cap
# in the Anthropic console actually bounds a bill.
# DAILY_ANSWER_LIMIT=200
